### 1. Introduction & Overview
Welcome to CleanMyPhone ("we", "our", or "us"). We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring you have complete control over your device's data. 

CleanMyPhone is engineered as a 100% On-Device, Privacy-First Storage Utility. All file indexing, duplicate photo detection, cache scanning, and storage analysis are performed strictly on your physical Android device. We do not collect, store, transmit, sell, or share any of your personal files, photos, videos, documents, or personal data with any third parties or remote servers.

---

### 2. Information We Process & How It Is Used
CleanMyPhone operates under strict Data Minimization principles. The application processes device data locally in temporary RAM to provide storage management utilities:
- Photos & Media: Analyzed locally using on-device image hashing algorithms to detect duplicate photos and burst shots. Never uploaded or shared off-device.
- Videos & Heavy Files: Read locally to calculate file sizes, durations, and formats for clutter management. Never leaves your device.
- System Cache & Temp Files: Scanned in local public/external storage directories to calculate recoverable space. Never leaves your device.
- Installed Applications: Package metadata (app name, package ID, APK size, install date, last used timestamp) is read to identify large or inactive apps. Never leaves your device.
- System RAM & CPU Metrics: Read in real time from Android Linux system kernels (/proc/stat, ActivityManager) to display live device performance. Never leaves your device.
- Network Speed / Bandwidth: Live data transfer rates are calculated via TrafficStats to provide the real-time speedometer tool. Never leaves your device.
- User Preferences: Scan settings, dark mode preferences, and notification toggles are stored locally using Android DataStore / SharedPreferences.

---

### 3. Permissions & Justification
- All Files Access (MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE): Required on Android 11+ to scan, index, and delete residual junk files, obsolete APK installers, orphan cache files, duplicate downloads, and large files across the internal shared storage. Only files explicitly confirmed by the user in the Cleanup Basket are modified or deleted.
- Read Media Permissions (READ_MEDIA_IMAGES, READ_MEDIA_VIDEO, READ_MEDIA_AUDIO, READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE): Allows the app to display photo thumbnails, group identical/burst photos for review, and list large video files. Media files are never uploaded or indexed off-device.
- Query All Packages (QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES) & Usage Stats (PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS): Powers the Applications Hub and Inactive Apps Manager by calculating storage consumed by installed applications and identifying apps unused for 30+ days.
- Accessibility Service (BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE): An optional, user-initiated utility that automates navigating to system App Info screens to clear app cache files for user-selected applications. The service is disabled by default, active only during user-initiated cache clearing, and never captures, stores, or transmits keystrokes, passwords, or personal screen content.
- Notifications (POST_NOTIFICATIONS): Used solely to deliver local alerts when recoverable storage exceeds user-defined limits or when a scan finishes.

